WikiGOLF uses content from Japanese Wikipedia (https://ja.wikipedia.org/)
in two ways:

  1. Bundled data: Assets/data/jawiki_sdow-*.sqlite (article titles/links
     used for course generation).
  2. Live data fetched at runtime from the Wikimedia API while the game
     is running (article text, tables of contents and inter-article
     links via https://ja.wikipedia.org/w/api.php and
     https://ja.wikipedia.org/api/rest_v1/, plus article images served
     from https://upload.wikimedia.org/).

Wikipedia's text content (both the bundled data and anything fetched
live via the API) is dual-licensed under:

  * Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International License
    (CC BY-SA 4.0) - https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
  * GNU Free Documentation License (GFDL)
    - https://www.gnu.org/licenses/fdl-1.3.html

You may reuse this content under either license, at your choice.

Images loaded from upload.wikimedia.org (Wikimedia Commons) are NOT
covered by the above: each file carries its own license set by its
uploader (commonly CC BY-SA, CC0/public domain, or other free licenses,
and occasionally non-free "fair use" licenses restricted to Wikipedia
itself). Consult the individual file's page on commons.wikimedia.org
for its specific license and required attribution before reusing an
image outside of this game.

Access to the Wikimedia API is subject to the Wikimedia Foundation's
Terms of Use (https://foundation.wikimedia.org/wiki/Policy:Terms_of_Use)
and User-Agent policy
(https://meta.wikimedia.org/wiki/User-Agent_policy); this game identifies
itself as "WikiGOLF/1.0 (https://github.com/aptmara/WikiGOLF)".

